## Approved Proposal Production Constraints

- Lock the official table of contents and submission constraints first.
- Give technical requirements the greatest feasible one-to-one physical-page visibility.
- Protect business-understanding and strategy pages.
- Compress integrable quality, management, and support content only when requirement visibility remains.
- Prepare the final cross-reference table near the end and use it as the final requirement-coverage audit.
- Distinguish legitimate working-deck residue from final-submission errors.
- Treat design as an expression tool without independent content-change authority.
- Have AER provide review findings and improvement direction rather than fixed detailed rewrite instructions.
- Use qualitative residual-defect disposition; no precise numerical acceptance formula is required.

These constraints guide downstream Production Layer implementation. They do not modify AER Core or constitute a complete authoring implementation.

Deferred or non-core:

- exact page-author action sequence,
- exact proposal-manager review sequence,
- A3 production or merge ownership and software, and
- causal contribution of specific pages to proposal awards.

