## Adopted: Cognitive-Load-Reduction Interaction Architecture

DEC-006 and SESSION-012 adopt a non-Core interaction architecture that preserves the complete canonical reasoning state while reducing the amount presented to the human at one time.

The approved structure is:

```text
AER Core canonical reasoning state
→ Safety Mediation Layer
→ Cognitive Projection Layer
→ Human Interaction Layer
→ explicit CONTINUE / REVISE / REOPEN / NEW_SCOPE transition
→ updated canonical state and audit trace
```

The interaction architecture separates canonical, projection, and interaction state; uses Level 1–3 progressive disclosure; provides Delta, Conflict, and Hold views; and presents one blocking question at a time while preserving queued dependencies.

Display limits are not reasoning limits. Hidden information is not deleted. Human acknowledgment is not evidence validation, and selection is not automatic Final Conclusion. Existing Link Governance, use authority, validation states, Bottleneck logic, tiered Runtime selection, and Global Impact and Consistency Closure remain unchanged.

This adoption does not implement a user interface, external agent, RAG system, or Proposal Production Layer. Time saving and decision-quality improvement are not current acceptance metrics. Implementation code and repeated actual-work usability validation remain deferred.

